[
  {
    "sha": "83a397d1b7e34b2f117a281f60b8c861dcf7b84b",
    "node_id": "C_kwDOVqp2oNoAKDgzYTM5N2QxYjdlMzRiMmYxMTdhMjgxZjYwYjhjODYxZGNmN2I4NGI",
    "commit": {
      "author": {
        "name": "Riley Porter",
        "email": "rileyporter@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-10T16:57:02Z"
      },
      "committer": {
        "name": "Riley Porter",
        "email": "rileyporter@gmail.com",
        "date": "2026-11-11T13:25:16Z"
      },
      "message": "feat(post): Synthetos TinyG post processor and generic 3-axis machine\n\nA new built-in post, \"TinyG\" (assets/posts/tinyg.cps), for Synthetos TinyG\ncontrollers running the edge-next firmware, and a generic \"TinyG 3-axis\"\nmachine. Specced from TinyG's public wiki (Gcode Support, Homing and\nLimits, Flow Control and Footers, Inch and Millimeter Units Mode) and the\nLinuxCNC G-code reference, behaviour only; structured after grblhal.cps.\n\n- Header G21|G20 G17 G90 G91.1 G94 G64: the words M30 does not reset on\n  TinyG. No %, O word, N numbers, G40, G49 or tool length word.\n- Z lift (G53 only when the machine states safe_retract, else the work\n  offset clearance, refused by name when unknown or buried), then\n  `T<n> M6` alone and `M0` on its own line: TinyG's M6 moves nothing, so\n  the stop is the operator's tool change. Tools 1-31; a larger number is\n  refused by name.\n- No canned cycles: drilling posts as its plain-move chain with `G4 P<s>`\n  at the hole bottom; tapping, control/wear compensation, going home and\n  tilted moves are refused by name; probing is refused by the engine.\n- Comments drop the characters the serial input acts on (! ~ % / { $),\n  lines are kept under 191 bytes, lengths are written at four decimals.\n\nEvery golden under golden/nc/tinyg/ and synth_tinyg.nc replays through the\nedge-next firmware's own parser and planner (build 450.03) with no refused\nline. Pinned by tinyg_post (11 tests), conformance, and the cross-post\nsuites after_op, comment_escape, control_comp, wear_comp, coolant,\ncoolant_followups, fanuc_post, inverted_post, machine and post/tests/comp.\n\nStacked on #715 (grblHAL post), which it extends the same lists as.\n\nFixes #836",
